===  Six major verbal patterns ===
There are six major verb stems or verbal patterns (binyanim) in Jewish Babylonian Aramaic.  The form ''pe‘al'' (פְּעַל) “to do”, the form ''Aph'el'' (אַפְעֵל) “let do”, and the form ''Pa'el'' (פַּעֵל) “like to do”,  are all in the active voice. But the  form ''Itpe'el'' (אִתְפְּעֵל), the form ''Itaph'al'' (אִתַפְעַל) and the form ''Itpa'al'' (אִתְפַּעַל) are essentially reflexive and usually  function in a passive sense.<ref>{{harvnb|Frank|2011|p=18}}: "A survey of the aramaic binyanim"</ref><ref>{{harvnb|Frank|2011|p=23}}: "Talmud Bavli Aramaic"</ref>

